WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.811
Open the Assembly tab. Parts come together here and can move.

00:00:07.361 --> 00:00:11.460
Click Insert. Both Part Studios are listed.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:18.848
Click Skateboard Deck and Trucks, then the green check. Don't click the window.

00:00:19.398 --> 00:00:25.470
Right-click the deck → Fix.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:34.762
Select the 3 truck parts → Fix. (The lesson text uses fastened mates.)

00:00:35.312 --> 00:00:39.341
Second truck: in the Part Studio, open Mirror.

00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:47.275
Pick the 3 truck parts, Right plane, New (not Add).

00:00:47.825 --> 00:00:54.884
In the assembly, insert the 3 new parts, then Fix them.

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:59.962
Insert Wheel and Bearing. It lands in the middle.

00:01:00.512 --> 00:01:05.550
Select wheel + bearing → Group.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.643
Hide the deck to see the axles.

00:01:09.193 --> 00:01:19.038
Revolute mate: hover the hanger end until the connector appears, click.

00:01:19.588 --> 00:01:23.211
Click the bearing face. The wheel jumps onto the axle.

00:01:23.761 --> 00:01:26.466
Insert Wheel and Bearing 3 more times.

00:01:27.016 --> 00:01:33.099
Widen the panel. Wheel 2 goes with Bearing 2, and so on.

00:01:33.649 --> 00:01:38.444
Group each pair: 2, 3, 4.

00:01:38.994 --> 00:01:42.106
Revolute the next wheel to the other truck.

00:01:42.656 --> 00:01:50.585
Shift+7, then the arrow keys to turn the view.

00:01:51.135 --> 00:01:55.663
Wheel over the hanger? It's backwards.

00:01:56.213 --> 00:02:00.985
Click Flip primary axis.

00:02:01.535 --> 00:02:05.215
Same for the last wheel.

00:02:05.765 --> 00:02:12.754
Show the deck. Two trucks, four wheels. Drag a wheel: it spins.

00:02:13.304 --> 00:02:20.503
Your complete skateboard. Challenge: add bolts and nuts from Standard content.
